WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.813
The second gap was in
the de-duplication key.

2
00:00:02.813 --> 00:00:07.200
The script de-duplicated on
source, subject and drift class.

3
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.989
So if two attributes drifted on one user,

4
00:00:09.989 --> 00:00:13.538
say department and manager,
they became one record.

5
00:00:13.538 --> 00:00:16.394
The second finding's
intended state was lost,

6
00:00:16.394 --> 00:00:18.787
and the re-read checked only the first.

7
00:00:18.787 --> 00:00:22.625
Now the key adds the attribute
whenever the payload names one.

8
00:00:22.625 --> 00:00:26.875
You'll see it in the lab: Erin's finding
has a key that ends in department.

9
00:00:26.875 --> 00:00:30.967
Two attributes drifting on one
subject are now two findings,

10
00:00:30.967 --> 00:00:34.813
each with its own intended state,
and a node test pins that.

11
00:00:34.813 --> 00:00:38.780
The kit's README and the
implementation example both say so.
